==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|deico}} {{qual|archaic}}

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|la|deyḱ}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*deikō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*déyḱti||to show, point out}}. The perfect forms are derivated from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*dḗyḱst}}.

Cognates include Oscan {{m|osc|𐌃𐌄𐌝𐌊𐌖𐌌||to show, point out}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|दिशति|tr=diśáti}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|δείκνυμι}} and Old English {{m|ang|tǣċan}} (English {{m|ang|teach}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|dīcō}}
* {{audio|la-cls-dico-long.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|dīcō|dīcere|dīxī|dictum|conj=3|pattern=short-imp}}

# I [[say]], [[utter]]; [[mention]]; [[talk]], [[speak]].
#: '''''Dixit''' duas res ei rubori fuisse.''
#:: He '''said''' that two things had abashed him.
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Genesis|1|3|quote='''dixit'''que Deus fiat lux et facta est lux|trans=And God '''said''': Be light made. And light was made.}}
# I [[declare]], [[state]].
## I [[affirm]], [[assert]] (positively).
# I [[tell]].
#* '''c. 254–184 {{B.C.E.}}''', [[w:Plautus|Plautus]], [[w:Captivi|Captivi]] ("The Captives"), 623, ([http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm English and Latin text])
#*: Eho '''dic''' mihi, quis illic igitur est?
#*:: Hey? '''Tell''' me, who is he then?
# I [[appoint]], [[fix]], [[name]] (to an office).
# I [[call]], name.
# {{lb|la|legal|followed by ad}} I [[plead]] (before).
# I speak in [[reference]] to, [[refer]] to.

=====Inflection=====
{{la-conj-irreg|dico}}
Old forms:
* paragogic infinitive present passive: {{m|la|dīcier}}
* singular imperative present active: {{m|la|dīce}} (= {{m|la|dīc}})
* gerundive: {{m|la|dīcundus}} (= {{m|la|dīcendus}})
* indicative future active: {{m|la|dicebo}}, {{m|la|dicebit}} <!-- length? -->

=====Synonyms=====
